# Milestone: M6 Wave 3 (v0.6.2 — Phase 5 / Gap #1)
# Covers: closure cross-session call stability; the regression fixed in Phase 5:
#         a closure compiled in one REPL session and installed as a realm-global
#         must remain callable in subsequent REPL sessions after its originating
#         UModule is destroyed.
#
# Because the .chk runner drives everything in a single urbi process, the
# pure cross-chunk scenario -- a closure built by one urbi_run call and
# called by the next -- has no C-level case of its own today; the file
# that used to hold it went with the old core.  The nearest standing
# coverage is tests/rt/test_exec.c::upvalue_outlives_defining_frame, which
# pins the capture itself but within one chunk.
#
# UModule no longer exists either: a closure keeps its chunk alive through
# its root proto's back-pointer, so "after its originating module is
# destroyed" is now "after nothing else refers to the chunk".
#
# This fixture validates single-session nested closure construction so that any
# bytecode-level regression in the OP_CLOSURE origin_nested path is caught
# before it would affect cross-session calls in the REPL.

var mk = function() { var x = 42; function() { x } }; var get_x = mk(); get_x()
[00000001] 42
